---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  AlertDialogConfirmations,
  AlertDialogPending,
  AlertDialogPlayground,
  AlertDialogProgress,
  AlertDialogReview,
  AlertDialogSizes,
  AlertDialogUnsaved,
} from "../../components/AlertDialogDemo";
---

<Docs
  title="Alert Dialog"
  description="Confirmations that interrupt the person and wait for an answer."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Alert Dialog</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A modal question before something hard to undo: delete, disconnect, leave,
    or discard. Outside clicks do not close it. Focus stays inside until the
    person answers, then returns to where it was.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8" id="alert-dialog-demo">
    <AlertDialogPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Alert dialog usage"
      code={`import {
  AlertDialog,
  AlertDialogAction,
  AlertDialogCancel,
  AlertDialogContent,
  AlertDialogDescription,
  AlertDialogFooter,
  AlertDialogTitle,
} from "@tulipfarm/sprout/alert-dialog";

<AlertDialog open={confirmStop} onOpenChange={(value) => { if (!busy) setConfirmStop(value); }}>
  <AlertDialogContent>
    <AlertDialogTitle>Stop this plan?</AlertDialogTitle>
    <AlertDialogDescription>
      Unfinished tasks are cancelled and saved agents pause. Finished work is kept.
    </AlertDialogDescription>
    {error && <p role="alert" className="text-sprout-danger">{error}</p>}
    <AlertDialogFooter>
      <AlertDialogCancel disabled={busy}>Keep running</AlertDialogCancel>
      <AlertDialogAction variant="destructive" disabled={busy} aria-busy={busy} onClick={stop}>
        {busy ? "Stopping…" : "Stop plan"}
      </AlertDialogAction>
    </AlertDialogFooter>
  </AlertDialogContent>
</AlertDialog>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>AlertDialog</code> works controlled with <code>open</code> and <code
        >onOpenChange</code
      >, uncontrolled with <code>AlertDialogTrigger</code>, or mounted only
      while open with <code>open</code> fixed to true. Ignore the change in <code
        >onOpenChange</code
      > to block Escape while work is pending.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>AlertDialogCancel</code> closes the dialog. <code
        >AlertDialogAction</code
      > is a <code>Button</code> and does not close it, so close it yourself on success
      and keep it open to show progress or an error.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Sizes</h2>
    <p>
      <code>size</code> is <code>"default"</code> (20rem, 24rem from 640px) or <code
        >"sm"</code
      > (20rem). With <code>AlertDialogHeader</code>, a default dialog puts <code
        >AlertDialogMedia</code
      > beside the text from 640px; <code>sm</code> always centers it and splits the
      footer into two equal buttons.
    </p>
    <AlertDialogSizes client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Confirmations</h2>
    <p>
      Most confirmations place the title and description straight in the content
      without a header. Cancel can run its own <code>onClick</code>, for example
      to clear a pending choice.
    </p>
    <AlertDialogConfirmations client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Pending and errors</h2>
    <p>
      Disable both buttons and set <code>aria-busy</code> on the action while work
      runs. Show errors as a <code>role="alert"</code> paragraph or an <code
        >Alert</code
      > inside the dialog. When the result is known, hide the action and let Cancel's
      label say what happens next.
    </p>
    <AlertDialogPending client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Progress</h2>
    <p>
      A plain <code>Button</code> in the footer can start work that runs inside the
      dialog, with a <code>role="status"</code> count.
    </p>
    <AlertDialogProgress client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Review changes</h2>
    <p>
      Pick the action variant from what confirming does, and disable it when the
      review is out of date.
    </p>
    <AlertDialogReview client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Unsaved changes</h2>
    <p>
      Guard navigation away from a dirty draft. Pass <code>finalFocus</code> a function
      when focus should land somewhere other than the trigger.
    </p>
    <AlertDialogUnsaved client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="alert-dialog-api">
    <h2 class="section-title">API</h2>
    <p>
      <code>AlertDialog</code>, <code>AlertDialogTrigger</code>, <code
        >AlertDialogPortal</code
      >, <code>AlertDialogOverlay</code>, <code>AlertDialogTitle</code>, and <code
        >AlertDialogDescription</code
      > wrap the Base UI alert dialog parts and take their props, including <code
        >render</code
      >. <code>AlertDialogHeader</code>, <code>AlertDialogFooter</code>, and <code
        >AlertDialogMedia</code
      > render a <code>div</code> and accept <code>render</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>AlertDialogContent</code> takes <code>size</code>, <code
        >container</code
      >, and every Base UI popup prop such as <code>initialFocus</code> and <code
        >finalFocus</code
      >. <code>AlertDialogAction</code> takes every <code>Button</code> prop. <code
        >AlertDialogCancel</code
      > takes Base UI close props plus <code>variant</code> (default <code
        >"outline"</code
      >) and <code>size</code>. <code>alertDialogSizeNames</code> lists the sizes.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The popup has <code>role="alertdialog"</code>, is named by <code
        >AlertDialogTitle</code
      >, and described by <code>AlertDialogDescription</code>. Tab and Shift+Tab
      stay inside, Escape closes it unless you ignore the change, and outside
      clicks never close it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Opening fades and scales in over 180ms; closing takes 120ms. Both turn off
      when reduced motion is requested.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Alert dialogs use <code>--sprout-overlay</code>, <code
        >--sprout-surface</code
      >, <code>--sprout-canvas</code>, <code>--sprout-secondary</code>, <code
        >--sprout-line</code
      >, <code>--sprout-text</code>, <code>--sprout-muted</code>, <code
        >--sprout-shadow-overlay</code
      >, and <code>--sprout-radius-panel</code>. They need no brand color, so
      neutral and TulipFarm themes look alike in light and dark mode.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
